# Splunk Universal Forwarder Configuration

## Overview

The Splunk Universal Forwarder is a lightweight agent responsible for collecting Windows Event Logs and forwarding them to Splunk Enterprise.

Unlike Splunk Enterprise, the Universal Forwarder performs no indexing or searching. Its sole purpose is to reliably collect endpoint telemetry and deliver it to a central SIEM.

---

# Purpose

The Universal Forwarder enables centralized log collection by continuously monitoring Windows Event Logs and forwarding newly generated events.

This architecture closely resembles enterprise environments where thousands of endpoints send telemetry to one or more SIEM servers.

